%S A400525 0,1,2,0,1,0,1,2,0,1,4,1,2,0,1,0,2,0,1,5,0,1,2,0,1,3,0,1,0,1,1,2,1,3,
%T A400525 0,1,2,0,6,0,1,2,0,1,3,0,2,0,1,0,1,2,0,1,3,1,2,0,1,5,2,0,1,3,0,1,2,0,
%U A400525 1,4,0,1,0,1,0,1,1,7,0,1,2,0,3,0,1,2,0,1,4,0,2,1
%N A400525 The exponent of the highest power of 2 dividing the number preceding the n-th squarefree number.
%C A400525 A permutation of A339813.
%C A400525 The asymptotic density of the occurrences of k is 1/3 for k = 0, and 1/(3*2^(k-1)) for k >= 1.
%H A400525 Amiram Eldar, <a href="/A400525/b400525.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 2..10000</a>
%F A400525 a(n) = A007814(A005117(n)-1).
%F A400525 a(n) <= A399089(n).
%F A400525 Asymptotic mean: Limit_{m->oo} (1/m) * Sum_{k=2..m} a(k) = 4/3.
%t A400525 IntegerExponent[Select[Range[2, 151], SquareFreeQ] - 1, 2]
%o A400525 (PARI) list(kmax) = for(k = 2, kmax, if(issquarefree(k), print1(valuation(k-1, 2), ", ")));
%o A400525 (Python)
%o A400525 from oeis_sequences.OEISsequences import iterfun, squarefreepi
%o A400525 def A400525(n): return (~(m:=iterfun(lambda x:int(n+x-squarefreepi(x)),n)-1)&m-1).bit_length() # _Chai Wah Wu_, Oct 02 2026
%Y A400525 Cf. A005117, A007814, A023506, A339813, A399089, A400524.
%K A400525 nonn,easy,new
%O A400525 2,3
%A A400525 _Amiram Eldar_, Sep 29 2026
